A||N||3||costly86gt||major stereo problems||||9||
Z||000000||costly86gt||04-13-2000||04:35 PM||||I have a custom stereo which consists of 2 4x10's in the front infinity 4x6's in the back, a 5x25 sub box a blaupunkt head and a 12 disc blau. in the trunk, and also a 400wt. amp.My problems are that i have terrible noise interference and also that the changer doesn't always work on hot days. The biggest problem is that the sound will cut off but the head unit will stay on. This problem happens at any noise level so I don't think it's the amp. Please help, my car is to loud to listen to all the time.||||reg||9
Z||000001||olympic||04-13-2000||11:47 PM||||Hmmmm, your CD changer will shut down if it gets too hot or if the humidity goes over 95%, this is a built in safety feature in most cd players.  You may have to move it or find a way to get some cool air in there.<BR>   Does the noise interference you talk about go up and down in pitch with the engine rpm?  If so, a common cause is bad wiring techniques.  The amps' power wire must go directly to the battery(8 gauge or large in your case) and the amps' ground must attach to the frame or a solid metal panel that is attached to the frame.  Remember to remove any paint and dirt where you attach the amps' ground cable.<BR>    If your wiring is good, unhook the RCA inputs at the amp, if the noise disappears, the noise is coming from the RCA's or the head unit.  Try rerouting the RCA's away from anything else electrical, especiallly spark plug wires and the coil.  Also check the ground wire for the head unit.  It must be grounded as good as the amp.  A noise filter from Radio Shack for the head unit may help.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-14-2000||01:08 AM||||Also make sure the amps and other equipment are grounded at the same point and the same gage wire as the power. Make sure the ground strap from the engine block to the right side trunk lid mount is there. Don't run your power wires next to the low level RCA lines. Finally make sure the power wires don't go near the ECM harness. These are some of the common noise problems.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||04-14-2000||01:21 PM||||make sure the rcas and power wire arent side by side too.||||reg||1
